From f89e73d4d9a512711fc0d9000e3a67282390869b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:28:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] rpc: hand the JSON-RPC service to an embedder in-process

An application that embeds the node, and already has a transport of its
own between its processes, needs the JSON-RPC methods rather than a port
and a cookie.

RpcServer::in_memory_service() builds the service RpcServer::start()
serves, with the same methods, limits and RPC middleware, so error codes
stay zcashd's. run_node() takes an optional sink that receives it, before
the lightwalletd sink. StartCmd::start passes None, so zebrad itself
behaves as before.

With a sink, the stop RPC refuses, over TCP too: on Regtest it raises
SIGINT in the whole process, which is the embedding application.
